NOTICE - Reverse Engineering Disclosure
========================================

This Home Assistant integration for Water.io smart bottles was developed through
reverse engineering of the Water.io Android application for interoperability
purposes only.

Legal Basis
-----------
Reverse engineering for interoperability is generally legal under:
- EU Software Directive (91/250/EEC) Article 6
- US Copyright Law fair use doctrine (17 U.S.C. § 107)
- Interoperability exemptions in most jurisdictions

Methodology
-----------
1. Decompiled Water.io Android APK (versions 3.5.0 and 4.8.6) using JADX
2. Analyzed decompiled Java/Kotlin source to understand BLE protocol
3. Documented protocol opcodes, packet structures, and command sequences
4. Implemented independent Python code from scratch (clean-room implementation)
5. No Water.io source code was copied or incorporated

What Was Reverse Engineered
----------------------------
- BLE GATT service/characteristic UUIDs
- Command/response opcodes (e.g., 0x3C = GET_CAP_STATE)
- Packet structure: [opcode, 0x00, 0x00, payload_len, ...payload]
- TypeConfig TLV protocol for settings (type-length-value encoding)
- Log entry format and interpretation

What Was NOT Copied
--------------------
- No Water.io source code
- No proprietary algorithms (firmware does all ADC→mL conversion)
- No trade secrets beyond protocol observation
- No circumvention of encryption or DRM (protocol is unencrypted)

